# Docker build context excludes. Nothing here reaches the build engine, so it can
# never end up in a prod image. The build installs its own deps and compiles from
# source under apps/*, so host build outputs and dev/planning artefacts are noise.

# Deps & build outputs — the image runs `pnpm install` + build itself
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.pnpm-store
# tsc -b incremental cache — if copied in while `dist` is excluded, tsc thinks the
# package is already built and skips emit → @qlhs/contracts has no dist/*.d.ts and
# the web/api build fails with TS2307. Never ship it into the build context.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests & e2e — belong in git, never needed to RUN the app in prod
apps/api/test
apps/web/e2e
apps/web/.playwright
.playwright-mcp

# Planning / design / docs / generated maps — dev-only, huge, unused at runtime
_bmad
_bmad-output
docs
design-previews
graphify-out
vbsec-reports
Img
*.png
*.md
!apps/*/README.md

# Backups & DB dumps
backups
data_backups

# Secrets & certs — must never be baked into an image (mounted at runtime instead)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
pmh.com.vn
TEST-ACCOUNTS.md

# VCS, CI, editor
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
